From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:21:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: apple,t6041-aop: Add T8132

The T8132 (M4) AOP runs the same firmware transport as the T6041 one, and
its bootloader hands it over the same way. It also programs the AOP DART's
address filter (DAPF) and reserves the filter's windows, which the firmware
reaches through its DART at their physical addresses. The windows come in
memory-region with the firmware segments, up to 16 of them.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit c88ffc687063621c80be4f6dbb5b962a87ba9d38)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml   | 29 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml
index e8a2df8050..8e940d46e6 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/soc/apple/apple,t6041-aop.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Apple T604x Always-On Processor
+title: Apple T604x and T8132 Always-On Processor
 
 maintainers:
   - Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
@@ -16,9 +16,15 @@ description:
   reaches its services through the RTKit endpoints. The firmware's external
   code and log segments live in DRAM, and the bootloader reserves them.
 
+  On T8132 the bootloader also programs the AOP DART's address filter (DAPF)
+  and reserves its windows, which the firmware reaches through its DART at
+  their physical addresses.
+
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: apple,t6041-aop
+    enum:
+      - apple,t6041-aop
+      - apple,t8132-aop
 
   reg:
     minItems: 2
@@ -47,11 +53,12 @@ properties:
 
   memory-region:
     minItems: 1
-    maxItems: 4
+    maxItems: 18
     description:
-      The firmware segments in DRAM (its external code and its log), filled in
-      by the bootloader from the ADT. The iommu-addresses property of each
-      region gives the address the firmware uses for it.
+      The firmware segments in DRAM (its external code and its log) and, on
+      T8132, the DAPF windows, filled in by the bootloader from the ADT. The
+      iommu-addresses property of each region gives the address the firmware
+      uses for it.
 
   audio:
     type: object
@@ -93,6 +100,16 @@ required:
   - mbox-names
   - iommus
 
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: apple,t6041-aop
+    then:
+      properties:
+        memory-region:
+          maxItems: 4
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
